<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The masses, in kg, of <m>8</m> sacks of maize at a cereals depot in Eldoret are</p><p style="text-align:center;"><m>{91},\ {97},\ {89},\ {96},\ {100},\ {98},\ {98},\ {94}</m></p><p>Use the assumed mean <m>A = {94}</m> kg.</p><p>(a) Find <m>\Sigma d</m>, where <m>d = x - A</m>.</p><div><m>\Sigma d =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the mean mass, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div>Mean <m>=</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> kg  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>With an assumed mean, subtract the same number <m>A</m> from every value to get the deviations <m>d = x - A</m>, keeping their signs. Subtracting the same number <m>A</m> from every value moves the mean down by <m>A</m> and leaves the spread unchanged, so the mean of the deviations, <m>\Sigma d \div n</m>, is how far the true mean lies above (or below) <m>A</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Mass <m>x</m> (kg)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{91}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{97}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{89}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{96}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{100}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{98}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{98}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{94}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>d = x - {94}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) Adding the deviations, <m>\Sigma d = {11}</m>.</p><p>(b) <me>\bar{x} = A + \frac{\Sigma d}{n} = {94} + \frac{ {11} }{8} = {95.375}</me>The mean mass is about <m>{95.4}</m> kg.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>11</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{763}{8}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>